2026-06-06 01:10:23 [http-nio-8080-exec-2] DEBUG c.d.w.s.e.WikipediaIngestionService - Wikipedia API response body: {"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"grncontinue":"0.131268550412|0.131271879782|24473457|0","continue":"grncontinue||"},"query":{"pages":{"56998318":{"pageid":56998318,"ns":0,"title":"Odontomachus clarus","extract":"Odontomachus clarus is a species of ant in the family Formicidae. It is endemic to Florida scrubs on the Lake Wales Ridge in Florida.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Odontomachus_clarus_casent0104735_dorsal_1.jpg/500px-Odontomachus_clarus_casent0104735_dorsal_1.jpg","width":500,"height":377},"pageimage":"Odontomachus_clarus_casent0104735_dorsal_1.jpg"},"56237773":{"pageid":56237773,"ns":0,"title":"No Strain","extract":"No Strain is an album by American blues pianist Memphis Slim which was recorded in 1960 and released on Bluesville, a sublabel of Prestige Records. It was reissued by Fantasy in 1972 as part of the double LP Raining the Blues, along with Just Blues, another album from the same sessions."},"34439993":{"pageid":34439993,"ns":0,"title":"The Loser List (series)","extract":"The Loser List is a series of fiction books by Holly Kowitt. The main character is Danny Shine."},"4450311":{"pageid":4450311,"ns":0,"title":"Viral envelope","extract":"A viral envelope is the outermost layer of many types of viruses. It protects the genetic material in their life cycle when traveling between host cells. Not all viruses have envelopes.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/CMVschema.svg/500px-CMVschema.svg.png","width":500,"height":344},"pageimage":"CMVschema.svg"},"47554543":{"pageid":47554543,"ns":0,"title":"Lonad","extract":"Lonad is a village in the Thane district of Maharashtra, India. It is located in the Bhiwandi taluka."},"56349657":{"pageid":56349657,"ns":0,"title":"1997 Rugby League Premiership","extract":"The 1997 Rugby League Premiership Trophy was the 23rd and final end of season Rugby League Premiership competition and the second in the Super League era. Following this season it was merged into the Super League Championship so one true national champion could be determined.\nThe winners were Wigan Warriors."},"55676703":{"pageid":55676703,"ns":0,"title":"1993–94 Roller Hockey Champions Cup","extract":"The 1993–94 Roller Hockey Champions Cup was the 30th edition of the Roller Hockey Champions Cup organized by CERH.\nIgualada won their second consecutive title."},"16519751":{"pageid":16519751,"ns":0,"title":"Botokoni","extract":"Botokoni is a village in the Ouham region in the Central African Republic.\nNearby towns and villages include Benesa (1.4 nm), Bankara (2.2 nm), Bouan (1.4 nm) and Galimel (1.4 nm)."},"62716159":{"pageid":62716159,"ns":0,"title":"List of wound decorations by country","extract":"This list of wound decorations is an index of articles that describe notable awards given for wounds; usually, though not exclusively, to military personnel during wartime. Decorations can include wound stripes, medals, or other uniform adornments.\nMedals are given to wounded soldiers to honor their sacrifices, create meaning for the pain they experience, and create a heroic identity for the wounded.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/Blesses_civils.PNG","width":218,"height":472},"pageimage":"Blesses_civils.PNG"},"60221189":{"pageid":60221189,"ns":0,"title":"Ministry of Commerce (Saudi Arabia)","extract":"The Ministry of Commerce (Arabic: وزارة التجارة) is a government ministry in Saudi Arabia that oversees commercial activity in the Kingdom and develops policies related to trade and the business sector.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/%D9%85%D8%A7%D8%AC%D8%AF_%D8%A8%D9%86_%D8%B9%D8%A8%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%84%D9%87_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%82%D8%B5%D8%A8%D9%8A.jpg","width":293,"height":320},"pageimage":"ماجد_بن_عبدالله_القصبي.jpg"},"97179":{"pageid":97179,"ns":0,"title":"Bastet","extract":"Bastet or Bast (Ancient Egyptian: bꜣstt), also known as Ubasti or Bubastis, is a goddess of ancient Egyptian religion, possibly of Nubian origin, worshipped as early as the Second Dynasty (2890 BCE). In ancient Greek religion, she was known as Ailuros (Koine Greek: αἴλουρος, lit. 'cat').\nBastet was worshipped in Bubastis in Lower Egypt, originally as a lioness goddess, a role shared by other deities such as Sekhmet.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Bastet.svg/500px-Bastet.svg.png","width":500,"height":1081},"pageimage":"Bastet.svg"},"49338579":{"pageid":49338579,"ns":0,"title":"Michael Roskin","extract":"Michael G. Roskin (1939 – May 2, 2023) was an American political scientist best known for his multi-edition textbook, Countries and Concepts."},"79799730":{"pageid":79799730,"ns":0,"title":"Edward Stenzel","extract":"Edward Antoni Stenzel (10 June 1846 – 15 April 1910) was the Polish pharmacist from Kolomyia,  businessperson and cavalier of the state title \"Aptekarski radcy cesarski\" (1898). He was a father of the famous pharmacist from Kolomyia and Lviv Stefan Stenzel.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Edward_Stenzel%27s_grave.jpg/500px-Edward_Stenzel%27s_grave.jpg","width":500,"height":744},"pageimage":"Edward_Stenzel's_grave.jpg"},"36887999":{"pageid":36887999,"ns":0,"title":"Kathy Foster","extract":"Kathy Foster may refer to:"},"15732843":{"pageid":15732843,"ns":0,"title":"List of Superfund sites in Idaho","extract":"This is a list of Superfund sites in Idaho, United States of America, as designated by the United States Environmental Protection Agency under the Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation, and Liability Act (CERCLA).  CERCLA, passed by Congress in 1980, authorized EPA to create a list of polluted locations requiring a long-term response to clean up hazardous-material contamination.  These locations are designated as Superfund sites, and are placed on EPA's National Priorities List (NPL)."},"7627279":{"pageid":7627279,"ns":0,"title":"New York State Route 268","extract":"New York State Route 268 (NY 268) is a state highway located in southwestern Delaware County, New York, in the United States. It runs from NY 97 in Hancock north over 10 miles (16 km) to a bridge over Cannonsville Reservoir near the former site of the hamlet of Apex in Tompkins. There, it ends at a junction with NY 10.","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/NY-268.svg/500px-NY-268.svg.png","width":500,"height":400},"pageimage":"NY-268.svg"},"53851673":{"pageid":53851673,"ns":0,"title":"New Zealand Wills Masters","extract":"The New Zealand Wills Masters was a golf tournament held in New Zealand played from 1965 to 1967. The Wills Classic had been held in New Zealand in 1963 and 1964. A Wills Masters tournament was also held in Australia from 1963."},"9909031":{"pageid":9909031,"ns":0,"title":"Max Bielschowsky","extract":"Max Israel Bielschowsky (20 February 1869 – 15 August 1940) was a German neuropathologist born in Breslau.\nAfter receiving his medical doctorate from the Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München in 1893, he worked with Ludwig Edinger (1855–1918) at the Senckenberg Pathology Institute in Frankfurt-am-Main. At Senckenberg he learned histological staining techniques from Carl Weigert (1845–1904).","thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Max_Bielschowsky.jpg/500px-Max_Bielschowsky.jpg","width":500,"height":731},"pageimage":"Max_Bielschowsky.jpg"},"68846918":{"pageid":68846918,"ns":0,"title":"Terminal digit preference","extract":"Terminal digit preference, terminal digit bias, or end-digit preference is a commonly-observed statistical phenomenon whereby humans recording numbers have a bias or preference for a specific final digit in a number. In medical science, this is often seen when recording measurements such as blood pressure by hand, where those taking measurements will round to the nearest 5 or 0. The phenomenon  has been blamed for misdiagnoses."},"6199774":{"pageid":6199774,"ns":0,"title":"Perak Turf Club","extract":"Perak Turf Club is the major Thoroughbred horse racing facility in Ipoh, Perak, Malaysia. The Club is a part of the Malayan Racing Association. [1]\nThe Perak Turf Club was established in 1884; it was the first exclusive turf club ever built in Perak."}}}}
